From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xun2202 <98207886+Xun2202@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 04:57:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] downloads: never drop a chapter silently; reuse or
 replace folders left on disk
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Tapping "download" on a chapter did nothing when a folder (or .cbz) for it
already existed on disk although the chapter list showed it as not
downloaded: Downloader.queueChapters filtered such chapters out with a
storage lookup and returned nothing, so the button flashed and the queue
stayed empty. On 卓易通 this happens after an interrupted finalisation
(process frozen or killed while the pages were being moved into the final
folder) because the download cache only learns about folders on its hourly
renewal.

- queueChapters decides "already downloaded" from the download cache (the
  same information the chapter list shows) and reports what happened:
  queued / already downloaded / already in the queue / source not
  installed.
- downloadChapter checks the disk right after the page list is known: a
  complete folder or archive (page count >= pages) is registered in the
  cache as downloaded without re-downloading, an incomplete leftover is
  removed and the download starts from scratch. Temporary directories are
  only created afterwards.
- The manga screen shows a snackbar when chapters were not queued, with
  the reason.

Shared helper isCountedPageFile() keeps the completeness rule in one place.
Anikku has the same filter in queueEpisodes (anikku-harmony 0018).
